WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.478
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B one.

2
00:00:05.778 --> 00:00:09.188
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.488 --> 00:00:17.028
Unit thirty-four: Future Continuous and Future Perfect. Today you will describe actions in progress or completed at a future time.

4
00:00:17.328 --> 00:00:19.957
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:24.121
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.983 --> 00:00:26.089
Will be doing.

7
00:00:27.083 --> 00:00:30.314
Will be doing means an action in progress at a future time.

8
00:00:30.917 --> 00:00:32.533
At six I will be cooking.

9
00:00:33.117 --> 00:00:35.502
Your turn. Say: Will be doing.

10
00:00:38.367 --> 00:00:39.403
Will be doing.

11
00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:41.302
Will have done.

12
00:00:42.317 --> 00:00:45.605
Will have done means an action completed before a future time.

13
00:00:46.217 --> 00:00:48.007
I will have finished by six.

14
00:00:48.617 --> 00:00:51.466
Your turn. Say: Will have done.

15
00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:55.452
Will have done.

16
00:00:56.217 --> 00:00:57.276
By then.

17
00:00:58.283 --> 00:01:00.469
By then means before or at that time.

18
00:01:01.083 --> 00:01:02.328
By then I'll be gone.

19
00:01:02.917 --> 00:01:05.081
Your turn. Say: By then.

20
00:01:07.933 --> 00:01:08.900
By then.

21
00:01:09.650 --> 00:01:10.779
By the time.

22
00:01:11.783 --> 00:01:14.561
By the time means before a certain future event.

23
00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:17.417
By the time you arrive, I'll have left.

24
00:01:18.017 --> 00:01:21.226
Your turn. Say: By the time.

25
00:01:24.067 --> 00:01:25.335
By the time.

26
00:01:26.083 --> 00:01:27.386
In progress.

27
00:01:28.383 --> 00:01:31.126
In progress means happening and not yet finished.

28
00:01:31.717 --> 00:01:33.449
The work is in progress.

29
00:01:34.050 --> 00:01:36.668
Your turn. Say: In progress.

30
00:01:39.533 --> 00:01:40.801
In progress.

31
00:01:41.550 --> 00:01:42.481
Completed.

32
00:01:43.483 --> 00:01:45.111
Completed means finished.

33
00:01:45.717 --> 00:01:47.287
The project is completed.

34
00:01:47.883 --> 00:01:50.431
Your turn. Say: Completed.

35
00:01:53.267 --> 00:01:54.291
Completed.

36
00:01:55.050 --> 00:01:56.051
Next year.

37
00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:59.398
Next year means the year after this one.

38
00:01:59.983 --> 00:02:01.704
Next year I'll graduate.

39
00:02:02.317 --> 00:02:04.563
Your turn. Say: Next year.

40
00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:08.436
Next year.

41
00:02:09.183 --> 00:02:10.068
Deadline.

42
00:02:11.083 --> 00:02:13.721
Deadline means the last time to finish something.

43
00:02:14.317 --> 00:02:15.898
The deadline is Friday.

44
00:02:16.483 --> 00:02:19.310
Your turn. Say: Deadline.

45
00:02:22.167 --> 00:02:23.191
Deadline.

46
00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:27.361
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:28.217 --> 00:02:31.377
Visal, what will you have achieved by the end of this year?

48
00:02:32.483 --> 00:02:40.662
By December I will have finished two English courses. The future perfect shows an action completed before a future time.

49
00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:43.575
And the future continuous?

50
00:02:44.683 --> 00:02:56.972
It shows an action in progress at a future time: This time next week I will be travelling. Will be doing means the action will be happening at that moment.

51
00:02:58.083 --> 00:02:59.920
How do time expressions help?

52
00:03:01.017 --> 00:03:18.498
By, by then, by the time and before often go with the future perfect: By the time you arrive, I will have left. At, this time tomorrow go with the future continuous. Use present tense after by the time.

53
00:03:19.633 --> 00:03:21.482
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:22.317 --> 00:03:25.907
Grammar focus: Future continuous and future perfect.

55
00:03:26.207 --> 00:03:27.417
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:28.117 --> 00:03:30.824
This time next week I will be travelling in Thailand.

57
00:03:31.717 --> 00:03:34.610
By December I will have finished two courses.

58
00:03:35.517 --> 00:03:37.876
By the time you arrive, she will have left.

59
00:03:38.833 --> 00:03:46.481
Will be doing = in progress at a future moment. Will have done = completed before a future moment. Use the present after by the time.

60
00:03:47.217 --> 00:03:51.123
Be careful! Don't say: By Friday I will finish already.

61
00:03:53.067 --> 00:03:55.438
Say: By Friday I will have finished.

62
00:03:55.738 --> 00:03:57.250
Use the future perfect.

63
00:03:58.033 --> 00:04:00.558
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:01.367 --> 00:04:02.530
At That Time.

65
00:04:02.830 --> 00:04:06.002
This time next week I will be travelling in Thailand.

66
00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:10.056
By December I will have finished two English courses.

67
00:04:11.067 --> 00:04:13.623
By the time you arrive, my sister will have left.

68
00:04:14.633 --> 00:04:18.003
The deadline is Friday, so the work will be completed by then.

69
00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:21.731
Next year I will be studying at university.

70
00:04:22.833 --> 00:04:26.475
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:27.317 --> 00:04:29.606
This time tomorrow I blank on a plane.

72
00:04:29.906 --> 00:04:33.467
A, will be sitting. B, will have sat. C, sit.

73
00:04:37.033 --> 00:04:39.044
The answer is A: will be sitting.

74
00:04:40.183 --> 00:04:42.636
By 2030 she blank her degree.

75
00:04:42.936 --> 00:04:48.075
A, will have finished. B, will be finish. C, finishes.

76
00:04:51.633 --> 00:04:54.086
The answer is A: will have finished.

77
00:04:55.250 --> 00:04:57.749
By the time he blank, we will have eaten.

78
00:04:58.049 --> 00:05:01.958
A, will arrive. B, arrives. C, arrived.

79
00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:07.383
The answer is B: arrives.

80
00:05:08.550 --> 00:05:10.666
Which means 'finished before that time'?

81
00:05:10.966 --> 00:05:14.654
A, will be working. B, will have worked. C, works.

82
00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:20.571
The answer is B: will have worked.

83
00:05:21.717 --> 00:05:24.424
According to the reading, when is the deadline?

84
00:05:24.724 --> 00:05:28.262
A, Friday. B, Monday. C, tomorrow.

85
00:05:31.800 --> 00:05:33.602
The answer is A: Friday.

86
00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:37.545
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:38.383 --> 00:05:40.662
What will you have achieved by the end of this year?

88
00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:50.985
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:51.285 --> 00:06:03.063
By the end of this year I will have finished my English course and I will have learned about two thousand new words. This time next year I will be preparing for a bigger exam.

90
00:06:03.363 --> 00:06:04.886
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:05.783 --> 00:06:10.769
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and future continuous and future perfect.

92
00:06:11.069 --> 00:06:15.184
Today's value is ambition. Dream big and work hard for your future.

93
00:06:15.484 --> 00:06:18.230
See you in Unit thirty-five. Goodbye!

94
00:06:18.530 --> 00:06:21.019
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

